  "cover_text": "If the summation of data production rate T(t) and amount of space B(t) at time t years is given by the formula T(t) - 2B(t) = 40 and initially, T(0) = 2 and B(0) = 3, what is the production rate at time t? The relationship given is:\n\n\\[\nT(t) - 2B(t) = 40\n\\]\n\nWe are also given the initial values:\n\n\\[\nT(0) = 2 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad B(0) = 3\n\\]\n\nFirst, let's substitute the initial values into the equation to see what it implies:\n\n\\[\nT(0) - 2B(0) = 40\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the given values:\n\n\\[\n2 - 2(3) = 40\n\\]\n\nSimplify:\n\n\\[\n2 - 6 = 40 \\implies -4 = 40\n\\]\n\nThis shows",
